/-!
# LMFDB level-1 modular form orbit `1.278.a.{a..}` (Hecke field degree 22)

The Hecke field `K = ℚ(α)` is degree 22 over ℚ. The LMFDB lists q-coefficients as
elements of `K`, which we decompose as `c_0 + c_1 · α + … + c_{21} · α^21`.
The combined form is `f = f_0 + α · f_1 + … + α^21 · f_{21}`, with each
`f_j` a level-1 weight-278 form with rational coefficients in `(E₄, E₆)`.

The Sturm bound for weight 278 is `⌊278/12⌋ + 1 = 24`. After certifying agreement
on the first 24 q-coefficients, `ModularForm.eq_of_sturm_bound` lets us conclude that any
form with the same coefficients equals our explicit `lmfdb_1_278_a_orbit`.

Generated by `scripts/lmfdb_qexp_to_e4e6_v3.sage`.
-/

